# ═══ 🚨 DO NOT DELETE — WITHOUT THIS FILE THE PRODUCTION BUILD FAILS ═══════════════════════════
#
# This is not a convenience. It is load-bearing for `npm ci`, which is what Netlify runs.
#
# THE CONFLICT. @circle-fin/developer-controlled-wallets v10 declares an OPTIONAL peer
# `@solana/codecs-strings@^2.0.0`. Our tree already has `@solana/codecs-strings@5.5.1` hoisted at
# the root, pulled in by the `@solana/kit` v5 family via @circle-fin/adapter-solana-kit. npm tries
# to satisfy the peer at the root, 5.5.1 does not match ^2.0.0, and the install dies with ERESOLVE.
# The peer is optional and we use none of the Solana path — Arc/EVM only — but npm still refuses.
#
# ⭐⭐ WHY THE FLAG MUST LIVE HERE AND NOT JUST IN THE COMMAND THAT BUILT THE LOCK.
# `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --package-lock-only` produces a correct, surgical lock. But
# **plain `npm ci` RE-VALIDATES PEER DEPENDENCIES AND REJECTS THAT LOCK** with the very same
# ERESOLVE. Netlify runs `npm ci`. So a lock resolved with the flag, without this file, installs
# fine locally and FAILS THE PRODUCTION BUILD — the flag has to be in scope at install time, for
# every install, which is what an .npmrc does and what a one-off command line does not.
# Verified 2026-08-29: plain `npm ci` fails without this file and succeeds with it.
# See [[lockfile-is-the-authoritative-install]] — package.json is not authoritative for what installs.
#
# ⚠️ THE COST, STATED PLAINLY. This disables peer-dependency enforcement REPO-WIDE and
# PERMANENTLY, for every future install — not just for the Circle SDK. npm will no longer tell us
# about a genuinely incompatible peer anywhere in the tree. That is a real loss of a safety net,
# accepted knowingly.
#
# THE ALTERNATIVE THAT WAS DECLINED. A clean re-resolution (delete the lock, resolve from scratch)
# succeeds with NO flag and needs no .npmrc — but it churns **90 version changes, 49 packages
# added, 39 removed**, across every money path: the whole Circle SDK suite (app-kit 1.8.1→1.13.0,
# bridge-kit, swap-kit, provider-cctp-v2), viem 2.52.2→2.56.0, axios, plus DOWNGRADES
# (@noble/curves 1.9.1→1.4.2, cross-fetch 4.1.0→3.2.0, eventemitter3 5.0.1→4.0.7). That is not a
# dependency bump; it is a tree replacement, and it would need its own proof. Rejected on that
# basis, not because it does not work.
#
# ⭐ IF YOU WANT THIS FILE GONE, the way out is to remove the conflict, not the flag: drop the
# Solana adapter (@circle-fin/adapter-solana-kit) so nothing hoists @solana/codecs-strings@5.x, or
# take the full re-resolution above with a proof to match. Deleting this line alone breaks deploys.
legacy-peer-deps=true
